  "text": "The body remembers what the mind forgets. Clay holds the shape of a hand. Light travels without memory. A machine dreams in the dark. Every touch is a kind of writing. We walk along the edge of memory. The wind scatters names. Dust learns the language of rain. Somewhere a door is still open. Your shadow arrives before you do. Silence has a weight and a grain.",
